{
  "openapi": "3.0.2",
  "info": {
    "title": "STACKIT Secrets Manager Vault API (KV v2 and logins)",
    "version": "1.15.0",
    "description": "Trimmed from HashiCorp's published Vault OpenAPI document (hashicorp/vault-client-go openapi.json, Vault 1.15.0, read 2026-11-01) to what STACKIT Secrets Manager serves and the provider needs: KV v2 data and metadata, and the AppRole and userpass logins. Changes from the source, all to describe the wire: paths carry the `/v1` prefix the source leaves to its servers entry; the mount is one `mount` label (STACKIT mounts KV v2 at the instance id, docs.stackit.cloud/products/security/secrets-manager/how-tos/set-version-limit-for-secrets-manager); responses describe Vault's whole `{ data | auth }` envelope, which the source leaves to its Go client's wrapper; the login responses, which the source doesn't describe, and the error responses come from Vault's API docs and docs.stackit.cloud/products/security/secrets-manager/how-tos/handle-authentication-lockouts."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://prod.sm.eu01.stackit.cloud"
    }
  ],
